' F1 -- The transformation: lecture materials to structured educational content.
' HERO FIGURE. Chapter 1 (Introduction).
' Claim supported: the thesis title made visual. One opaque artefact in, a set
' of addressable, queryable learning objects out -- and the capabilities each
' output unlocks.
@startuml f1-transformation
!include _style.iuml

title From lecture materials to structured educational content

skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
}

rectangle "**INPUT** — one opaque artefact" as IN #F2F2F2 {
  rectangle "**Lecture slide deck (PDF)**\n1–300 pages\n----\n• text trapped in page layout\n• no slide boundaries as data\n• no notion of a //concept//\n• not addressable, not queryable\n• readable by humans, opaque to software" as A
}

rectangle "**TRANSFORMATION**" as MID #DCDCDC {
  rectangle "1. Extract\nper-page text (PyMuPDF)" as T1
  rectangle "2. Route\ntext-bearing vs image-only" as T2
  rectangle "3. Synthesise\nbatched LLM, 8 slides/call" as T3
  rectangle "4. Embed\n768-dim vectors" as T4
  T1 -[#1A1A1A]-> T2
  T2 -[#1A1A1A]-> T3
  T3 -[#1A1A1A]-> T4
}

rectangle "**OUTPUT** — addressable learning objects" as OUT #F2F2F2 {
  rectangle "**Slide records**\ntitle · body · summary\n//trust flags: needs_review, vision_routed//" as B1
  rectangle "**Quiz questions**\n4-option MCQ, one per slide\n//tagged by Bloom level + concept//" as B2
  rectangle "**Slide embeddings**\npgvector 768, HNSW index" as B3
  rectangle "**Deck metadata**\ntitle · summary · key topics" as B4
}

rectangle "**CAPABILITIES UNLOCKED**" as CAP #BFBFBF {
  rectangle "Grounded Socratic tutor\n//retrieval-scoped, citation-checked//" as C1
  rectangle "Spaced repetition\n//SM-2 over quiz-derived cards//" as C2
  rectangle "Mock exams\n//coverage-first, weakness-weighted//" as C3
  rectangle "Professor analytics\n//per-slide engagement//" as C4
}

A -[#1A1A1A]-> T1
T4 -[#1A1A1A]-> B3
T3 -[#1A1A1A]-> B1
T3 -[#1A1A1A]-> B2
T3 -[#1A1A1A]-> B4

B3 -[#1A1A1A]-> C1
B2 -[#1A1A1A]-> C2
B2 -[#1A1A1A]-> C3
B1 -[#1A1A1A]-> C4

note right of MID
  The transformation is **one-way and
  server-authoritative**: the database is
  the single source of truth for what a
  slide "is" once parsed
  (parser/persist.py:5). The client never
  supplies structured content — it can
  only correct it afterwards.
end note

legend bottom
  Every output object is independently addressable, which is what makes the
  capabilities on the right possible at all. The input PDF supports none of them.
endlegend

@enduml
